# Solidity checkout line endings are pinned per file, because solc's metadata hash — the
# fingerprint appended to bytecode and compared by `npm run check:deployed` — covers the source
# bytes including their line endings.
#
# The contracts deployed on 2026-10-02 were compiled from a working tree where most of these files
# were CRLF and two were LF. Without pinning, a Linux clone (no core.autocrlf) checked the LF ones
# out as LF and the CRLF ones as LF too, and a Windows clone did the opposite, so the same commit
# compiled to three different metadata hashes: CI reported drift while the deploying machine
# reported a match. `text` keeps the repository copy LF; these lines decide the bytes on checkout.
#
# A future redeploy should compile from a tree that is uniformly LF and then simplify this file.
*.sol text eol=lf

packages/contracts/contracts/ExecutionGuard.sol text eol=crlf
packages/contracts/contracts/PolicyManager.sol text eol=crlf
packages/contracts/contracts/SafeTreasuryGuard.sol text eol=crlf
packages/contracts/contracts/TreasurySafeShell.sol text eol=crlf
packages/contracts/contracts/interfaces/Enum.sol text eol=crlf
packages/contracts/contracts/interfaces/ITransactionGuard.sol text eol=crlf
